<title>GREECE: Greece to auction FRNs, fixed rate bonds Dec 27.</title>
<headline>Greece to auction FRNs, fixed rate bonds Dec 27.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece will auction 200 billion drachmas of FRNs and 100 billion of fixed-coupon bonds on December 27, the finance ministry said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The issue date for the bonds will be December 31, 1996. Rate details will be supplied later, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The finance ministry's next issue of T-bills is planned for January 2, 1997. The government has ended tax-exempt status for debt issues from January 1, 1997. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
